    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0013:0001",
      "blockId": "paragraph:discussion:0013",
      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "In the following example, the [`subscribe(on:options:)`](publisher/subscribe(on:options:).md) operator causes `jsonPublisher` to receive requests on `backgroundQueue`, while the [`receive(on:options:)`](publisher/receive(on:options:).md) causes `labelUpdater` to receive elements and completion on `RunLoop.main`.",
      "normalizedSource": "In the following example, the [`subscribe(on:options:)`](publisher/subscribe(on:options:).md) operator causes `jsonPublisher` to receive requests on `backgroundQueue`, while the [`receive(on:options:)`](publisher/receive(on:options:).md) causes `labelUpdater` to receive elements and completion on `RunLoop.main`.",
      "sourceHash": "4308b09947211cdef91b5974e63d893c90cbe497c81e704e8446c45dcc3ef887",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "In contrast with [`subscribe(on:options:)`](publisher/subscribe(on:options:).md), which affects upstream messages, [`receive(on:options:)`](publisher/receive(on:options:).md) changes the execution context of downstream messages.",
      "contextAfter": "```swift\nlet jsonPublisher = MyJSONLoaderPublisher() // Some publisher.\nlet labelUpdater = MyLabelUpdateSubscriber() // Some subscriber that updates the UI.\n\njsonPublisher\n    .subscribe(on: backgroundQueue)\n    .receive(on: RunLoop.main)\n    .subscribe(labelUpdater)\n```",
      "documentTitle": "receive(on:options:)",
      "framework": "Combine",
      "ko": "",
      "status": "failed",
      "reviewed": false,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:code:discussion:0014:0001",
      "blockId": "code:discussion:0014",
      "type": "preserve",
      "source": "```swift\nlet jsonPublisher = MyJSONLoaderPublisher() // Some publisher.\nlet labelUpdater = MyLabelUpdateSubscriber() // Some subscriber that updates the UI.\n\njsonPublisher\n    .subscribe(on: backgroundQueue)\n    .receive(on: RunLoop.main)\n    .subscribe(labelUpdater)\n```",
      "normalizedSource": "```swift let jsonPublisher = MyJSONLoaderPublisher() // Some publisher. let labelUpdater = MyLabelUpdateSubscriber() // Some subscriber that updates the UI. jsonPublisher .subscribe(on: backgroundQueue) .receive(on: RunLoop.main) .subscribe(labelUpdater) ```",
      "sourceHash": "0d162b7c4b568194a23010a2e2a1ed4c8a00f1376fd59aee4b337f4349e9ffcd",
      "translatable": false,
      "preserveReason": "code",
      "contextBefore": "In the following example, the [`subscribe(on:options:)`](publisher/subscribe(on:options:).md) operator causes `jsonPublisher` to receive requests on `backgroundQueue`, while the [`receive(on:options:)`](publisher/receive(on:options:).md) causes `labelUpdater` to receive elements and completion on `RunLoop.main`.",
      "contextAfter": "Prefer [`receive(on:options:)`](publisher/receive(on:options:).md) over explicit use of dispatch queues when performing work in subscribers.",
      "documentTitle": "receive(on:options:)",
      "framework": "Combine",
      "ko": "```swift\nlet jsonPublisher = MyJSONLoaderPublisher() // Some publisher.\nlet labelUpdater = MyLabelUpdateSubscriber() // Some subscriber that updates the UI.\n\njsonPublisher\n    .subscribe(on: backgroundQueue)\n    .receive(on: RunLoop.main)\n    .subscribe(labelUpdater)\n```",
      "status": "preserved",
      "reviewed": false,
      "locked": true
    },
